{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>There is a generation</b> — \"generation, generation, generation, the leech\" (Prov. 30:11–15). These four things are joined in interpretation with the four daughters, and the proof of this: \"a generation that curses its father,\" \"an eye that mocks a father,\" \"the leech\" — it is like עות and it is fitting to be עקולה, from twisted judgment מעוקל, and it [the leech] is reversed [in letters] like כשב — כבש, ירעף — יערף. And two and three by way of lengthening:" "<b>Does not bless</b> — for she [the mother] has dealt kindly with him, and is worthy of blessing. And there is a generation that is pure and honored in its own eyes, yet does not wash its filth, that is: and one who cannot wash his flesh from his filth, where will he wash his heart from its evil? And he thinks that he is pure?! An allusion to the arrogant."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The comment cites letter reversals (עות/תוע, כשב/כבש, ירעף/יערף) tersely; translated literally without expansion. The phrase 'two and three by way of lengthening' is obscure and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:42.965794090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}